- How would you extend to multiple targets efficiently?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests interval DP, memoization, and bottom-up tabulation on a classic polygon triangulation problem with solution counting. It checks careful state design and combinatorial counting under optimal substructure.

## Key Concepts
- Interval DP on polygons: dp[i][j] = min over i<k<j of dp[i][k] + dp[k][j] + w[i]*w[k]*w[j]
- Counting optimal solutions: parallel cnt[i][j] updated when a new min is found or matched
- Circular handling: fix a root vertex and solve a linearized version

## Code Example
```javascript
function minTriangulation(w){
  const n = w.length;
  const dp = Array.from({length:n},()=>Array(n).fill(Infinity));
  const cnt = Array.from({length:n},()=>Array(n).fill(0));
  for(let i=0;i<n-1;i++){ dp[i][i+1] = 0; cnt[i][i+1] = 1; }
  for(let len=2; len<n; len++){
    for(let i=0; i+len<n; i++){
      const j = i+len;
      for(let k=i+1; k<j; k++){
        const val = dp[i][k] + dp[k][j] + w[i]*w[k]*w[j];
        if(val < dp[i][j]){ dp[i][j] = val; cnt[i][j] = cnt[i][k] * cnt[k][j]; }
        else if(val === dp[i][j]){ cnt[i][j] += cnt[i][k] * cnt[k][j]; }
      }
    }
  }
  return {minCost: dp[0][n-1], ways: cnt[0][n-1]};
}
```

Trie advantages: inserts/finds traverse a path matching the word, sharing prefixes reduces duplication; autocomplete across a prefix becomes a subtree traversal, yielding all completions efficiently. Hash maps store exact keys; prefix queries require scanning all keys or maintaining inverted indexes, which is costly. Trade-offs: Tries incur higher pointer/structural overhead per node and can be memory-heavy with large alphabets or sparse usage; compression (Patricia/radix) or fixed-size arrays can mitigate this. Deletion is non-trivial due to shared prefixes. Real-world nuance: store frequencies at nodes to surface top-k suggestions, or prune with a capped DFS for responsive UI.

